ces evidently couldn't get  enough of kerry talking nonsense to  animals  critics on the other hand mostly  wondered why the sequel didn't actually  try to improve on the first movie  for example the new york times janet  maslin wrote that  when nature calls has enough schoolboy  gags and pratfalls to keep aces least  demanding fans awake  but it doesn't have certain basics like  a screenplay  the bodyguard was a movie sold on the  strength of both its stars and an  all-time best-selling soundtrack  at 33 on the tomato meter however  critics didn't like much else about it  peter rayner of the los angeles times  summed up the prevailing view  just about everything that can go wrong  with this film does  and yet it's compulsively watchable so  was a train wreck  but kevin costner was a top five box  office draw in 1992  coming off the mega hit oscar champion  dances with wolves in 1990  as well as a crowd-pleasing comedy robin  hood prince of thieves  in 1991 his star would fall  precipitously throughout the 90s  after a series of epic misfires but in  that moment he was  box office gold as for whitney houston  the bodyguard may have been her  cinematic debut  but she was hardly a showbiz neophyte  houston was already a global pop star at  the time with a number of multi-platinum  albums and number one hits under her  spangled belt  it was her majestic voice that turned  the elegant but simple dolly parton tune  i will always love you into one of the  most cherished of all pop ballads  as well as one of the best selling songs  of all time together she and costner  pushed the film past critical objections  to more than 120 million dollars at the  domestic box office  if there was ever an unexpected box  office conqueror it was the 1990s home  alone  made without any real stars for a measly  18 million dollars the movie grossed  nearly 477 million dollars at the global  box office  as it turned out audiences went  absolutely wild for the fresh face kevin  mcallister  as